  "caveats": [
    "Phonetic bracket symbols in a vocal diction guide are reported options, not a demonstrated phonemic inventory or validated conversational realizations.",
    "The choral diction author explicitly adapts some symbols for singers; disagreement is not proof that any option is categorically wrong.",
    "Initial Pinyin b/d/g can be modeled as voiceless unaspirated stops despite singer-friendly voiced-label options.",
    "The 21-row Lin/Mei/Cai labels are attributed as reported by Cai; no independent examination of all Lin and Mei original publications is claimed.",
    "Six simple finals are compared, while 27 other written-final categories and 112 context-sensitive simple-final readings remain unresolved.",
    "i has distinct sibilant-conditioned values outside the plain i row, o may depend on preceding onset, and ü may carry a glide in a source author's notation.",
    "Zero independent human decoding or acoustic testing is implied by source transcription.",
    "The exceptional Mei Pinyin t entry is explicitly questioned by Cai; retain it as a reported table item, not an endorsed pronunciation."
  ]
}
